    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `checkDigit` field \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the `customerCode`.\n\nThe project follows a pattern where derived response fields are computed getters on the `Owner` entity and auto-mapped by MapStruct into the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`. Two changes fit that pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly integer 0\u20139), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `getCheckDigit()` derived getter that runs the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits in `customerCode` (ignoring the non-digit separators/letters), returning `null` when there's no customer code to guard other GET paths.\n\nMapStruct maps the new `checkDigit` property by name automatically (like the existing `locality`, `membershipLevel`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey` derived getters), so no mapper or pipeline changes were needed.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
