    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into an already-established pattern on `Owner`: a family of \"derived at response time, not persisted\" getters \u2014 `getLocality()`, `getContactPreference()`, `getIdentityKey()` \u2014 each documented with the same doc-comment idiom. `getCheckDigit()` is one more of exactly this kind, in the right unit (a computed property over `customerCode`, which lives on `Owner`), and its Javadoc matches the surrounding style closely.\n\n- Logic placement is correct: neighboring getters (`getLocality`, `getIdentityKey`) already embed their derivation inline (with small private helpers where warranted), so keeping the Luhn computation in the getter is consistent \u2014 there's no pre-existing utility or numeric-code home it's bypassing, and no duplication introduced.\n- The null-`customerCode` handling mirrors the defensive style of the other derived getters.\n- `Owner` isn't becoming a catch-all here \u2014 these are all cohesive identity/response-projection accessors, not unrelated responsibilities piling up.\n- The OpenAPI addition is placed among the other `readOnly` derived fields and described consistently with the Javadoc.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
